{
  "_about": "Implementations, each checked against its package registry before being written down.",
  "_method": "Every row resolved with a 200 from registry.npmjs.org or pypi.org/pypi. Six candidates 404ed and were dropped; five more resolved to unrelated projects sharing a name (PyPI `sdf` is Scientific Data Format, `wfc` is WebForms Core) and were dropped too.",
  "_caveat": "last_release is the registry timestamp verbatim. Many npm packages report 2022-05/06, which clusters too tightly across unrelated projects to be real activity — probably a bulk metadata operation. Do not read those dates as abandonment. One package (webaudio-oscilloscope) was removed entirely: it is a visualiser, not a generation library, and was only present because registry verification confirms a package exists without confirming it is the right kind of thing. Four others were re-roled for the same reason.",
